PART B - HELLOWORLD SMART CONTRACT
========================================

1. Open Remix IDE:
https://remix.ethereum.org

2. Create Solidity file:
HelloWorld.sol

3. Write the following code:

// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.0;

contract HelloWorld {

    string public message = "Hello Blockchain";

    function getMessage() public view returns(string memory) {
        return message;
    }
}

4. Open Solidity Compiler tab.

5. Compile HelloWorld.sol.

6. Open Deploy & Run Transactions tab.

7. Select Environment:
Remix VM

8. Click Deploy.

9. Expand deployed contract.

10. Click getMessage() function.

11. Verify output:
Hello Blockchain


========================================
PART C - ARRAY SMART CONTRACT
========================================

1. Create Solidity file:
ArrayDemo.sol

2. Write the following code:

// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.0;

contract ArrayDemo {

    uint[] public numbers;

    function addNumber(uint _num) public {
        numbers.push(_num);
    }

    function getNumber(uint index) public view returns (uint) {
        return numbers[index];
    }

    function getAllNumbers() public view returns (uint[] memory) {
        return numbers;
    }
}

3. Compile ArrayDemo.sol.

4. Open Deploy & Run Transactions tab.

5. Select Environment:
Remix VM

6. Click Deploy.

7. Use addNumber() to insert values.

8. Use getAllNumbers() to retrieve full array.

9. Use getNumber(index) to retrieve specific value.

10. Verify output successfully.
